Problem:  I sometimes have difficulty when wishing or otherwise because
I don't get the spelling quite right.

For example, I tried three times to wish for a "helm of brilliance"
before finally getting what I wanted by wishing for  a "helmet" of
brilliance.

I've had similar joys wishing for "grey dragon scale mail" instead of
"gray dragon scale mail",  "cloak of magic resistence" instead of
"cloak of magic resistance" etc.

Sooo ...

... rewrite engine to first look for exact match. If found, well and
good.  If not, does a regular expression match. (E.g. searches for
"*resist*" instead of "resistance", "Gr*y" instead of "gray" or "grey",
"*flayer" instead of "mind flayer" or "mindflayer").   Return possible
matches in dialog boxes. User selects match he meant.  This will allow
people to get their wish right even if they ask for it in a slightly
unusual form ("helm" instead of "helmet") or  variant spellings,
